{
  "id": "book-32",
  "checkpoint": 16,
  "title": "Packing the Gear",
  "summary": "Paul desmonta seu acampamento, organiza os itens dentro da mochila com cuidado e se despede dos amigos antes de iniciar a subida final.",
  "audio_url": "/audios/book-32.mp3",
  "word_count_target": 140,
  "story_en": "After finishing his hot drink, Paul returns to his campsite. He pulls the metal pegs from the dry soil and carefully folds the tent fabric into a compact roll. He secures it inside the lower compartment of his backpack.\n\nNext, he checks his equipment list. He arranges the heavy items close to his back to reduce pressure on his spine. He places his water canteen, map, and compass in the outer pockets for easy access.\n\nClara walks over, tightening the straps on her own rucksack. “Are you ready to depart?” she asks with a bright smile.\n\n“Everything is packed and balanced,” Paul replies, fastening the buckle around his waist.\n\nThey exchange warm farewells with the other campers. With light footsteps and a clear mind, Paul begins the final climb toward the highest mountain summit.",
